stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> SavedPreference
    SavedPreference --> DesktopDefault: No file or media override
    SavedPreference --> DesktopEntry: Saved application ID
    SavedPreference --> CustomCommand: Legacy or custom argv
    DesktopEntry --> Unavailable: Application ID is missing
    DesktopEntry --> Launch: Resolve current installed entry
    CustomCommand --> Launch: Resolve legacy entry or retain custom argv
    DesktopDefault --> Launch: xdg-open uses desktop MIME associations
    Launch --> TerminalChild: Terminal application
    TerminalChild --> Execute: Add the terminal execution option
    Launch --> Execute: File or media application
    Unavailable --> [*]: Show error
    Execute --> [*]
    note right of SavedPreference
        Burl preferences control Burl actions.
        Desktop MIME defaults and keybindings are separate.
        Store desktop IDs, not versioned executable paths.
    end note
